  },
  "sd": {
    "sck": 13,
    "mosi": 6,
    "miso": 3,
    "cs": 7,
    "hz": 20000000,
    "mount": "/sdcard"
  },
  "expander": {
    "type": "PCF8574",
    "sda": 8,
    "scl": 18,
    "address": 32,
    "active_high": false
  },
  "menu_action": "ui_cancel",
  "verified": true,
  "notes": "ESP32-S3FH4R2: 4 MB flash and 2 MB quad PSRAM in the package. Native USB (Type-C) for flashing and the serial log; TX/RX (GPIO43/44) stay free for an external USB-UART. GPIO26-37 are not broken out (in-package flash and PSRAM), GPIO21 drives the on-board WS2812. The default pins are a handheld wiring: display and SD card share one SPI bus (SCK IO13, MOSI IO6, two chip selects), buttons on a PCF8574 I2C expander (SDA IO8, SCL IO18) plus two direct buttons."
